<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kazakh famine of 1930–1933</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930–1933</span> · Also known as Asharshylyk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kazakh famine of 1930–1933, known in Kazakh as the Asharshylyk, was a man-made famine in Soviet Kazakhstan. Forced collectivisation, the settlement of nomads and heavy requisitioning of grain and livestock destroyed herds that most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> depended on. About 1.5 million people died, a large share of all Kazakhs, and many more fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and other parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kazakh-famine-of-1930-1933.jpg" alt="Kazakh famine of 1930–1933" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ds02006 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ALAGolod.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
